uplicate-scope point (cause 2, though not their permission list) and the \"tokens never expire\" point (cause 3).\n- **Not applied:** their claim that the token exchange must leave out `grant_type` and `redirect_uri`. Rivera's exchange worked with them included, so I didn't change it. I also kept our existing signed `state` instead of switching to a JWT, since it already does the same job.\n- **Not done:** encrypting tokens at rest and a guard against reconnecting to a different Intervals account. They're worth doing but didn't cause these failures.","ttft_ms":1858,"type":"result","duration_ms":89014,"uuid":"68b29f22-f368-45c8-acfc-9edd73187680","ttft_stream_ms":885,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":885,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":9179,"cacheReadInputTokens":236688,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22985,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4148616000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1696,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
